    "source": "\n**Frame:** Verso. Curt performs the final manuscript build. [Page 118](118.md) is still concealed by a black thumbnail.\n\n**Action:** Source packets, corrections, and uncertainty labels compile beside the reading edition. A cover proof reads `THE TWO ANTHILL PROBLEM`. Beside it, a discarded connected-hills sketch remains visible under a heavy cancellation stroke; the kept sketch has two separate surfaces and unmarked space between. A revision slip reads `9 SEPTEMBER 2026 — TITLE REVISION`. Neither sketch has a queen, chamber, or individual agent identity. A small print of the supplied Apache Ant logo hangs on the back wall, a reconstructed software-history prop. Reserve this print as blank space in model-generated base art and composite the supplied image afterward. Two tiny authored ants sit in the desk’s light; they do not stand for particular runs.\n\n**Dialogue — CURT:**\n> Two incidents. How many went unseen?\n\n**Screen / system text — CHATGPT:**\n> The picture cannot answer that.\n\n**Provenance:** `reconstructed` — project publication scene.\n\n",
    "title": "The title revision keeps the evidence boundary"
